Ladybird now counts the layout bounds of the inline boxes around
the root of a top- or bottom-aligned subtree in the line box, as
it does those of any other inline box. Blink places each inline
box in InlineLayoutStateStack, and unites its metrics with the
line box’s whatever its children are aligned to; only the boxes aligned
to the line box wait for its final size, as PendingPositions. WebKit
computes the line box from every inline box in LineBoxVerticalAligner::
computeLineBoxLogicalHeight(), with the top- and bottom-aligned
ones handled apart, and Gecko from every span in nsLineLayout::
VerticalAlignFrames(). Chrome 157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and
Playwright’s WebKit 26.5 ran the cases of the test added here, and agree
on all but one, where Chrome alone places a shifted box differently;
Ladybird gives what Firefox and WebKit give.
